    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nI would like to be able to select a block in visual mode and surround them with parenthesis or braces, and it should do a linebreak after the opening symbol and another after the block before closing. \r\n\r\nIt should look like this afterwards.\r\n\r\n```c\r\n(\r\n    printf(\"hello\");\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\ninstead of this.\r\n\r\n```c\r\n(printf(\"hello\");)\r\n```",
