        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "So I finally gave up on not adding this, since I managed to find a quite manageable implementation of this feature. In particular, I didn't know that indent/dedent can be conveniently done programmatically with `:[range] >` and `:[range] <` (see `:h :>`).\r\n\r\nThis functionality is not default and is activated with new `respect_selection_type = true` option. It changes how linewise and blockwise addition works along with deletion that looks like it should revert linewise add. I hated introducing new option for this, but I can see that this behavior is useful and breaking changes are bad.\r\n\r\nSee details [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/doc/mini-surround.txt#L555).",
